  "id": "performative",
  "term": "performative",
  "definition": "In this psychology context, performative refers to a form of social behavior shaped by perceived risk, where a person manages their emotions and outward expression to fit expected norms and avoid negative social or evaluative consequences. The packet discusses this specifically as part of performative relationality among neurodivergent people in workplace interactions.",
